[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every date report into one issue, because the desk merges on the
subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Read by cause, the reports hold
more than one problem. Each one below has its own ticket, with the reports it covers.

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

<Callout kind="warn">
Counts come from the desk's own rule in <code>src/lib/kb/causes.ts</code> and its notes in
<code>src/lib/data/desk-notes.json</code>, over the export of 4 October, built when the page renders.
</Callout>

### parser

The shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes the day first. A booking
for 7 April comes out as 4 July. This is the bug #4471 was opened for.

### hint

A different bug with no ticket of its own. Tenants on the booking-v3 form show `MM/DD/YYYY` under the
date field, so their people type the month first, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day
first. Fixing the parser does not fix these: the hint is wrong, not the parser.

### one-day shift

A different bug again. These reports have no day and month swap: the date is one day off, or differs by
where the reader is, as in "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." That points at time
zones or the day boundary, not at date order. The desk listed them as one-day moves and its table files them
under the parser by tenant, but the parser fix will not move them back a day.

## How to check

- The cause of a report is `causeOf` in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`, never the intake tag, which guesses
  from the reporter's browser.
- The export repeats some reports across overlapping pages; each id counts once (`uniqueById`).
- Each ticket lists the ids of the reports it covers.

